request.description:
One endpoint for stocks (auto/alpaca), Dukascopy instruments, Kalshi perpetuals (kalshi_perps), and Kalshi/Polymarket US event contracts. Use source and symbol for instruments; use source, contracts, start and end for events. Perpetual prices are normalized to USD per underlying unit using provider contract scaling. No missing bars are filled. Perpetuals allow at most 5000 rows and 20000 intervals per date range. Follow Dukascopy next_cursor with page_mode=true and identical settings. CSV export requires a completed unpaged range. Provider licensing and available history still apply.

Request schema:
```json
{
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "symbol"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "symbol": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "contractSymbol": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "auto",
            "alpaca",
            "dukascopy",
            "kalshi_perps"
          ],
          "default": "auto"
        },
        "price_side": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "bid",
            "ask"
          ],
          "default": "bid"
        },
        "page_mode": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "Dukascopy: retrieve bounded candle file pages; follow next_cursor using the same settings."
        },
        "cursor": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "start": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "end": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "timeframe": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "1min",
            "5min",
            "15min",
            "30min",
            "1h",
            "4h",
